// Package slog is the LoGOs twin of the standard log/slog text and JSON
// handler path.
//
// It reuses the log/slog data model as is: Level, Attr, Value, Record,
// Handler, HandlerOptions, Leveler, LogValuer and Source, together with
// every slog constructor (String, Int64, Uint64, Float64, Bool, Time,
// Duration, Any, Group, GroupAttrs and the Value constructors). A twin
// handler implements slog.Handler, so it plugs into slog.Logger and any
// existing handler chain, and a twin Logger wraps any slog.Handler.
//
// The twin formats attributes without the original's dynamic dispatch and
// without ...any boxing on the way in:
//
//   - TextHandler and JSONHandler format the scalar attribute kinds
//     (string, int64, uint64, float64, bool, duration, time) with plain
//     appends into a pooled buffer. Shared helpers in logos/rt/json
//     recognize byte slices in already-boxed values and detect typed
//     nil pointers during panic recovery. BytesOf converts statically
//     typed byte slices before boxing.
//   - Logger takes ...slog.Attr instead of ...any, so typed constructors
//     never box on the way in.
//   - JSON floats append through logos/rt/json instead of a pooled
//     json.Encoder, and JSON []byte values append base64 directly.
//   - Text quoting appends through strconv.AppendQuote into the record
//     buffer instead of converting through an intermediate string.
//
// Compatibility boundary: DiscardHandler, the default logger, SetDefault,
// NewLogLogger and every ...any entry point (Logger.Info and friends,
// Record.Add, slog.Group with ...any) stay where they are in log/slog and
// are intentionally absent here. Migrate Info(msg, args...) to
// InfoContext(ctx, msg, slog.String(...), ...) or LogAttrs on a slog.Logger
// wrapping the twin handler; migrate Record.Add(args...) to AddAttrs;
// migrate slog.Group(key, args...) to slog.GroupAttrs(key, attrs...).
// ReplaceAttr, WithAttrs preformatting, WithGroup, AddSource, LogValuer
// resolution, empty-group elision and the one-write-per-record guarantee
// behave exactly as in log/slog: the twin test suite replays the
// standard handler, text and JSON behavior tests against the standard
// handlers as oracle and requires byte-equal output.
//
// Allocation bound: the handler formatting path allocates nothing at any
// attribute count while the record fits the pooled 1 KiB buffer; records
// that outgrow it allocate only for buffer growth. Through the Logger,
// records with more than the five inline slog.Record slots add exactly
// the one slice-growth allocation that log/slog itself performs. Dynamic
// Any values (maps, slices and structs through encoding/json, fmt
// fallbacks, TextAppender and TextMarshaler payloads) may allocate exactly
// as the original does. WithAttrs preformatting allocates once per
// WithAttrs call, as in the original.
//
// The JSON invalid-UTF-8 escape follows the toolchain experiment through
// build-tagged files, exactly like src/logos/rt/json: \ufffd by default,
// a literal U+FFFD under GOEXPERIMENT=jsonv2.
package slog
